{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"agent_message","text":"The mitigation is submitted and accepted (`stage: mitigation`). User requests through `frontend-proxy` now return 200 in about 5 ms.\n\n**Root cause:** `product-catalog` had stopped serving products. Its DB connection was broken during the bad rollouts, so `/api/products` returned 500 and the frontend reported `Product Not Found`. The database itself was fine: `otelu` can read `catalog.products` with the password the init script sets.\n\n**Fix:** I ran `kubectl rollout restart deploy/product-catalog -n astronomy-shop`. The new pod loaded the current `product-catalog-db-conn` secret, and the API recovered.\n\n**Not changed:**\n- The `product-catalog` deployment still carries the manual restart annotation from revision 4 and the 64Mi memory limit. Neither looked like the cause, so I left them.\n- Early on, `product-reviews` logged a password auth failure for `otelu`. That came from a pod that was terminating, and the current pod is healthy."}}
